# Albion lore, myths and exploration talk (classic + Shrouded Isles, up to 1.65).
# Documented lore is said plainly; rumours, superstitions and inventions are said as belief, memory or argument.
# Named monsters are ones that live in this world. Lore only for the 70+ bosses: nobody here claims a kill.
# Above all: the old Albion belief that Avalon was hidden in Albion all along (the marsh, the mist, the Lady).

@kind ambient
@realm alb
@topic lore
@about place

# ---------------- Avalon was here all along (explorers and old avalonians) ----------------
@who Explorer
@levels *
i still think avalon was in the marsh the whole time and we just never found the door
[the|those] [sunken|half sunk] roman pillars in avalon marsh [lead somewhere|point somewhere|are not there for decoration], [mark me|i swear it]
the old guides said the marsh ran right up to the edges of avalon city. i walked every inch of it and never saw a wall
swim far enough west of adribard's retreat and the fog [gets thick as a wall|stops moving|goes very quiet]. never had the nerve to keep going
i swam circles round the marsh islands for an hour looking for a ruin no map shows. found nothing but slimes
isle of glass is an old name for glastonbury, and glastonbury [was always|has always been] [called|said to be] avalon. [just saying|draw your own lines]
the isles did not find avalon, they just [pulled back the curtain|lifted the mist|took the mist away]
by the time we crossed the water, avalon city was already rubble. [somebody|the drakoran] [got there first|knew the way before us]
[heard|my old guild swore] lady nimue walks the marsh at night because [the door to avalon is still out there|she still guards the way in]
avalon marsh after dark [feels like|is like] [walking through someone else's dream|a door left half open]
[the|that] marsh mist [sits in|never lifts from] the same spots [every night|for weeks]. [real fog moves|fog that never moves is a spell]
walked the shore of avalon isle and the same sunken pillars are there too. same builders, i'm sure of it
some say merlin hid avalon himself before he vanished, so nobody could loot it while he was away
anyone else think avalon was hiding in the marsh all along?
a whole race of mages does not come from a city that isn't there. avalon was hidden, not missing

@who NoLifer
@levels 25-50
i rolled an avalonian [the first week|at launch]. we had a homeland on the character screen and nowhere to go home to
the day the isles opened, half the avalonians [i knew|in the realm] [went straight to the ruins|ran for the boats] like pilgrims
before the isles, the nearest thing albion had to avalon was a name on a swamp
[i've|i have] [waited|sat] in the marsh [half the night|for hours] [just to watch|to see] lady nimue go by. [worth it|no regrets]

@who Socialite
@levels *
[heard|someone in camelot swears] the barkeeps [sold|were selling] avalon isle iced tea before anyone could sail there. [explain that one|curious, no]
had a whole argument in camelot about whether avalon moved or we just never looked. three hours, no winner
[a bard|a minstrel] [in camelot|at the tavern] [sings|has a song] that the lady of the lake [folded avalon into the mist|keeps avalon in her sleeve]. [lovely tune|i believe it]

@who Crafter
a tailor in camelot swears the old marsh stones are cut the same way as the walls in avalon city

@who Leveler
i get why explorers chase the avalon story, but marsh slimes give awful xp

@who Daredevil
i dare anyone to swim due west from lyonesse until the map runs out

# ---------------- Dartmoor, Golestandt and the lost knights ----------------
@who *
@levels *
sir arward took thirty knights into dartmoor. [all that came back|the only thing that came home] was a [scorched|singed] journal
the journal [fell out of the sky|came down out of a clear sky] at prydwen keep, [they say|so the scribes write]. one word [left on it|still legible]: golestandt
a roman lord and his whole household vanished in dartmoor back in uther's day. nobody asked twice
[those|the] boulders in dartmoor are not boulders. granite giants, and [they get up|some of them stand] when you [aren't looking|least expect it]
the stonecrush ogres eat granite. think about what that does to a sword
never say the dragon's name inside dartmoor. old raid leaders swear she listens

@who Explorer
there's a corner of dartmoor south of the ruins where the grass is all burnt. i turned back
they say moran the mighty keeps watch in dartmoor too. never got close enough to check

@who *
@levels 35-50
golestandt's breath [eats|burns off] your heat resist [before the second one lands|first], [which is mean|which is just rude]
my old guild swore the trick is to fight inside the ruins, because anyone outside draws the big breath
[the heralds call golestandt she|golestandt is a she, ask any bard], [but|and] half the raid stories i've heard [still say he|swear it's a he]
fifty respec stones from one dragon, they say. half the realm would go just for those
i heard a raid of seventy went in once and it was over in three minutes. dragon stories always end like that

@who NoLifer
@levels 40-50
when the dragons first woke, the whole realm stood around in dartmoor just to look

@who Leveler
@levels 35-50
dragon raids are hours of waiting for five minutes of breath. not worth it

@who Daredevil
@levels 20-50
i dare anyone to go look at golestandt and come back walking

# ---------------- Cardova and the nameless emperor ----------------
@who *
@levels 15-50
cardova holds a roman emperor nobody can name. cornwall is a strange place to bury an emperor
emperor seleucus in cardova [has a name|is named], so he can't be the nameless one. [the forgotten emperor is the real mystery|that leaves the forgotten emperor]
the spirit of the emperor, the forgotten emperor, emperor seleucus. that crypt has more emperors than rome ever did
i think the nameless emperor at cardova is the one the dead legions march for. nobody believes me
knock on the cardova door twice before you go in. it's tradition and the dead seem to like it

@who Crafter
an old crafter i know swears the coins in cardova have a blank face on them. never saw one myself

# ---------------- Stonehenge and Merlin's barrow ----------------
@who *
