merlin's barrow lies under salisbury, right under the stones
merlin isn't dead. the barrow's [empty|for show], mark me
[the shade of uther pendragon|uther's shade] walks the barrows [and not merlin|while merlin is nowhere]. [that tells you something|make of that what you will]
[heard|an old bard told me] wizard lichas was [merlin's apprentice|a student of merlin] who stayed behind [when the barrow was sealed|after merlin went]
heard the stones were raised for ambrosius aurelianus. his shade is out there somewhere
merlin left his staff behind. wizards don't leave their staff unless they mean to come back
the barrows are the only place in albion where the dead outrank the living
touch the stones at stonehenge for luck before a big raid. half the realm does it

