# ---------------- Edges of the map, drowned lands and things nobody explains ----------------
@who Explorer
@levels *
every map of albion ends in water, [but|and] the water doesn't end. [swim long enough|keep swimming] and [the world stops you|you hit the edge]
lyonesse was a drowned land. [on a still night|when it's quiet] [you can hear|some hear] [bells under the water|church bells under the sea]
i keep a [map|list] of every cave in albion nobody [talks about|names]. [it's longer than you'd think|it keeps growing]
the coast of cornwall hides caves you can only reach from the water. found two so far
the pixie queen in campacorentin holds court somewhere off the paths. i followed the giggling once
granddaddy longlegs is a real name in campacorentin and i refuse to explain further
there's a white horse walking salisbury. [old folks say|i heard] it's [the one carved into the hills|older than the stones]
cynewulf the ghostwalker is not a briton name. someone else's war ended in salisbury
they found inishail just off the coast and you can swim there. makes you wonder how many more islands are hiding out there
the spirit of lord emthoro still holds inishail. nobody knows who he was
anyone else ever swum out past the last island just to see what happens?

@who *
@levels 25-50
the vetusta abbey bell rings in the black mountains, they say. i wonder who it rings for
cailleach uragaig walks lyonesse. the old folk in cornwall won't say the name
there's a thing called draco magnificens in the pennines, they say. never seen it
coliath rules gwyddneau and nobody can tell me what it guards
hadrian's wall was built to keep something out. nobody agrees what
the eye of arawn in snowdonia watches the whole frontier, they say. i wave when i pass

@who Socialite
@levels *
the bards in camelot can't agree whether lyonesse sank in one night or over a hundred years. i side with one night

# ======================= Debate scenes: Albion lore =======================
@kind debate
@realm alb

@topic lore_avalon
@levels 1-50
@scene alb_lore_avalon_in_the_marsh
@role B type=Explorer
@role C type=Leveler,NoLifer
@role D type=*
A: {q} anyone else think avalon was hidden in the marsh all along? | {q} i get more sure every week: avalon was in the marsh the whole time | here's my theory. avalon never moved. it was in the marsh and we missed it
B: the old guides said the marsh ran right to the edges of avalon city. edges. of a city nobody could see | the first maps had the marsh running up to avalon city's walls. so where were the walls
C: or the mapmakers were drunk and the isle was always across the water | guides get things wrong. the city is on an island, we sailed there, done
B: then explain the sunken roman pillars. nobody builds columns in a bog for fun | and the pillars sinking in the mud? that's a city's front steps, not a swamp
D: and lady nimue walks that marsh every night. the lady of the lake doesn't patrol frogs | why would the lady of the lake walk a swamp after dark unless there's a door in it
C: she walks camelot hills too. is avalon under the hills now | she walks four zones a day. by that logic avalon is everywhere
?B: maybe it is. maybe the mist picks where it lets you through | maybe the mist moved the door when the drakoran came. i'd have hidden it too
A: no proof either way. i still check the fog every time i ride past | nobody can prove it. i'm swimming the marsh again this weekend anyway
~ 20
?C: bring a lantern and leave me out of it | have fun with the leeches

@topic lore_avalon
@levels 20-50
@scene alb_lore_avalon_why_a_ship
@role B type=NoLifer
@role C type=Explorer
@role D type=Socialite
A: if avalon was in albion all along, why did we need a boat to get there | {q} question for the avalon believers: if it was always here, why the ship
B: i played an avalonian from the first week. a homeland on the character screen and no road home | avalonian since launch. born in a city nobody could visit
C: it wasn't hidden on the map, it was hidden behind the mist. the ship just goes round the mist | the boat proves nothing. you sail around a spell, not through it
A: so the isle of glass sat off the coast all that time and nobody noticed | a whole island sat offshore for years and not one fisherman saw it
C: isle of glass is glastonbury's old name, and glastonbury was always avalon. the clue was on the dock | the landing is called the isle of glass. that's glastonbury, that's avalon. it was in the name
D: my minstrel friend says the lady lifted the mist the night the drakoran broke the city. too late to save it | i heard nimue let the mist fall when the city burned, so someone could come help
B: either way the city we came from is rubble. we found home and it was already ruined | the avalonians finally got home and found drakoran in the kitchen
A: hidden or not, the drakoran found it first, and that bothers me more | the drakoran knew the way before we did. who showed them
~ 25
?D: someone holding a leash, that's who | ask the inconnu, they always know more than they say

@topic lore_avalon
@levels 35-50
@scene alb_lore_xanxicar_the_lock
@role B type=NoLifer
@role C type=Explorer
@role D type=Leveler,Daredevil
A: here's a thought. xanxicar was under avalon before the drakoran ever showed up | {q} which came first, the city of avalon or the dragon under it
B: the city. mages don't build over a sleeping dragon on purpose | the city, obviously. nobody builds a library on top of a dragon
C: or they did it on purpose. the dragon was the lock and the mist was the door | maybe the mages wanted it there. two heads, one to watch each way
B: then the lock failed. the drakoran walked right in | some lock. the drakoran strolled in and burned the place
C: drakoran are dragon-men. maybe the dragon let its own kind through | dragon-men walking past a dragon guard. who do you think opened the gate
D: you two are arguing about a dragon that fills its own cave with lightning. leave it alone | whatever it guards, it guards it from a room full of lightning. pass
?A: a cave that fills with lightning if you stay too long. that's a timer on a door | a dragon that doesn't want guests to linger. that's the strange part
B: or a dragon with a temper. two tempers, actually | or it's just in a bad mood. both heads
C: say what you like. mist, a lady in the marsh, a dragon in the cellar. that's a locked house | i think avalon was hidden on purpose and xanxicar was part of it

@topic lore_dragon
@levels 30-50
@scene alb_lore_golestandt_he_or_she
@role B type=NoLifer
@role C type=Explorer,Socialite
@role D type=*
A: settle it for me. golestandt, he or she | {q} is golestandt a he or a she, my guild is split down the middle
B: she. the heralds say she, the bards say she, end of story | it's she. every herald and every song says so
C: every raid story i ever heard calls him he | half the raid tales i know say he. the old timers swear by it
B: raiders call everything he. they call the barrow wights he | anything with teeth is a he to a raid leader, that proves nothing
D: does it matter? the breath burns the same either way | the breath feels the same whether it's a he or a she
C: it matters to the bards. you can't write a ballad about an it | matters if you're the one writing the song
?D: write it as the dragon and keep everyone happy | just say the dragon. diplomacy
A: still split. i'm saying she to be safe, she might be listening | fine, she, in case it can hear us from dartmoor

@topic lore_cardova
@levels 15-50
@scene alb_lore_cardova_nameless_emperor
@role B type=Explorer
@role C type=NoLifer
@role D type=*
A: {q} who is the emperor nobody can name in cardova | random thought, how does a crypt hold an emperor nobody can name
B: the scribes wrote it plain. a roman emperor, buried in cornwall, name lost | cornwall buried an emperor and then forgot him. that's the whole record
C: but emperor seleucus is right there with a name on him | seleucus is down there and he has a name, so it isn't him
B: there's a forgotten emperor too, and a spirit of the emperor. three emperors, one name between them | seleucus, the forgotten one, the spirit. that crypt is crowded with emperors
D: maybe seleucus is the one they remembered and the forgotten one was the real ruler | i think the forgotten one is the true emperor and seleucus took his seat
C: or seleucus is a usurper's name carved over a real emperor's bones | or the name was scraped off and the guards made one up
?B: either way the praetorians down there still know who they serve. we don't | the dead legion knows. ask one, i dare you
A: so nobody knows and the dead won't tell. typical cornwall | no answers, just more emperors. classic cardova

@topic lore_merlin
@levels 25-50
@scene alb_lore_merlin_in_the_barrow
@role B type=NoLifer
@role C type=Explorer
@role D type=Socialite
A: merlin is not dead. i will die on this hill | {q} does anyone still believe merlin is in his barrow
B: then why is it called the barrow of merlin | his name is on the barrow. nobody names a tomb after the living
C: uther's shade walks down there, the king's wight too. nobody has seen merlin's | i've seen the shade of uther pendragon. never once a sign of merlin
A: exactly. an empty barrow with a famous name. he left | so it's empty. he walked out, like he always did
D: an old bard told me wizard lichas was his apprentice, left behind to keep the door | i heard lichas is the student who stayed when merlin sealed it
B: or lichas is what's left of the old man and nobody wants to say it | maybe lichas is merlin. tell me you haven't thought it
C: merlin would never go lich, he had better taste | merlin as a lich? he'd sooner be a toad
?D: he left his staff for us to guard. that's a man planning to come back | the staff is still our relic. he meant to collect it
A: believe what you like. i still nod to the stones when i pass | i'll keep checking the barrows. somebody has to

@topic lore_inconnu
@levels 20-50
@scene alb_lore_trust_the_inconnu
@role B type=*
@role C type=NoLifer
@role D type=Explorer
A: {q} do we actually trust the inconnu | honest question, should albion trust the inconnu at all
B: they fight beside us against the drakoran. good enough for me | they took the field with us on avalon. what more do you want
C: they fight for arawn. we're just pointed the same way for now | arawn wants his stolen dead back. we're the tool, not the friend
D: and the arawnites in the black mountains pray to the same lord. explain that one | there's an eye of arawn in snowdonia. if arawn is our friend why is he watching us
B: every god has fools who follow him wrong. we have them too | a lord with bad followers. sounds like half of camelot
C: when arawn gets his dead back he'll want payment. guess in what coin | allies with the lord of the dead? he'll send a bill, and it'll be souls
?D: i have never once heard an inconnu say thank you | the inconnu tell you when, never why
A: so we keep them close and keep one eye open | trust them, and count your fingers after
~ 20
?B: if an inconnu reads this channel we're all in trouble | careful, they hear more than they let on

@topic lore_green_knight
@levels 20-50
@scene alb_lore_green_knight_game
@role B type=Daredevil
@role C type=NoLifer
@role D type=Explorer
A: has anyone ever just talked to the green knight | {q} what is the green knight actually doing on the sauvage road
B: standing there daring someone to swing. i respect it | waiting for someone brave enough. that'll be me one day
C: the old tale says he offers a blow for a blow, and the second blow comes a year later | in the story you take his head off, he picks it up and books you for next year
