@topic lore_relics
@levels 1-50
@scene alb_lore_scabbard_not_blade
@role B type=NoLifer
@role C type=Explorer
@role D type=Socialite
A: why is the scabbard our relic and not excalibur itself | {q} how did albion end up with the scabbard and not the blade
B: the old tales say the scabbard was worth ten swords. whoever wore it didn't bleed | merlin called the scabbard the greater gift. it kept arthur from bleeding
C: the sword went back to the lake. the lady keeps it | the blade went into the water when arthur fell. it's the lady's now
D: lady nimue walks the marsh every night. maybe she's carrying it | i've seen nimue out in the marsh after dark. if she has the blade she hides it well
C: and nobody takes anything from her. con her once and you understand | conning her is enough. nobody's prying a sword out of those hands
A: the heralds did promise more relics once. i say the blade is the one they kept back | more relics were promised and never came. the blade's the missing one
B: the day excalibur is a relic, the mids will camp the marsh | if they ever add the blade i want to be holding it, not guarding it
?D: and the hibs will say the lady was one of theirs all along | hibs would claim she's an elf in a lake
A: until then, guard the scabbard and bow if you see her | for now, the scabbard. and a polite bow to the lady

@topic lore_oldest
@levels 20-50
