A: what's the oldest thing in albion, honestly | {q} oldest legend in albion, go
B: golestandt. she was in dartmoor before uther's roman lord got lost there | the dragon. a roman lord vanished in dartmoor in uther's day and she was already home
C: keltoi fogou. those stones were old when rome was a village | the fogou. the carvings aren't roman, they're older than anything with a name
D: the stones at stonehenge. they were up long before anyone buried a wizard under them | stonehenge. they put merlin under it because it was already ancient
B: dragons outlive stones. ask the granite giants | the granite giants are the stones, and even they keep clear of her
C: then the giants are the oldest. they're the hills that walk | then the giants win. they are dartmoor
?D: the lake is older than all of you. ask the afanc | llyn barfog had its monster before arthur was born
A: no winner. i'm writing it down as all of them, it's albion | no answer, as usual. albion is old all the way down

